  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1201 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nWe are in for an unseasonably mild start to the work week, owing to \nweak ridging and increasing warm advection, which will keep the \npleasant conditions in place. Daytime temperatures in the low 60s \ncan be expected for most, with some passing clouds and light winds \nthrough the first half of the week. Midweek and beyond, a shortwave \ntrof will dig into the Upper Midwest, bringing low-end precipitation \nchances as an associated cold front passes through. There remains \nuncertainty on moisture availability, with only 20-30% PoPs for \nareas south of Interstate 80 at this time. Overall, this doesn't \nlook to be a heavy/widespread rainfall event. Rather, it should be \nquick-hitting and light, with WPC currently favoring <0.10\". The \nmore noticeable change in weather will be with temperatures, as cold \nadvection behind the front will drop us into the upper 40s to near \n50 for the second half of the work week.",
